WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.396
By 2030, one in six of us will be over sixty. Many live alone.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.999
Loneliness is linked to nearly nine hundred thousand deaths a year.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.719
Wick turns the TV she already watches into care: one button, her rules.

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.872
Shaped by a real mother of seventy-nine, and her daughter.

5
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.559
Made for Fire TV: over two hundred and fifty million sold.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.880
This is Wick's project site. Here is how it is built.

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.376
The television renders, and never decides.

8
00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:34.508
Her Fire TV only draws cards. One button answers each.

9
00:00:34.908 --> 00:00:39.564
The edge checks every television, and answers Ring within five seconds.

10
00:00:39.964 --> 00:00:43.540
Strands agents on Bedrock AgentCore do the reasoning.

11
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.892
The MCP server gives Alexa plus twenty-six tools. The Guardian checks every word.

12
00:00:50.292 --> 00:00:53.220
Bedrock describes the door in one sentence.

13
00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.028
DynamoDB and S3 keep the home's story.

14
00:00:57.428 --> 00:01:00.356
Sarah sees only what her mother agreed to share.

15
00:01:00.606 --> 00:01:04.182
All in Terraform, deployed by GitHub Actions.

16
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:13.440
This is a real Fire TV Stick 4K Select, fresh out of the box. I installed Wick on it, and it opens on her home screen.

17
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.204
Sarah types the code on her TV. Margaret allows her with one press.

18
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.272
Sarah asks how her mum is. Wick answers from counted facts.

19
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.416
Her note waits for a natural break. Margaret answers with one button.

20
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.904
A second note appears the moment the film pauses.

21
00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:04.516
When someone rings, a card appears over the film. Maria, a parcel, movement, or a stranger. Ask Sarah to look sends her the picture.

22
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.872
Sarah sends a picture. It arrives at a quiet moment.

23
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:25.520
She arranges the window cleaner's visit. Their phone says on the way, late, at the door, and her TV says so.

24
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:37.384
Watch together. Margaret says yes, and Sarah sits down to the same film.

25
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.992
Hold OK for two seconds, and Sarah is asked to ring.

26
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.206
Her light shows her day has begun.

27
00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:01.556
Sarah asks for Spanish, and Margaret says yes on her TV. Then back to English.

